/P 1194 0 R
/E (the first step of creating the ER Diagram, we identified the main entities required for the airline reservation and travel management system. These entities were converted into tables that represent the core components of the database. The tables include Users, Travelers, Trips, Tickets, Payments, Reviews, Airlines, Airports, Seats, and SeatReservations. Each table was created to store specific information related to the system, such as user data, trip details, payment records, airline information, and seat bookings. After identifying the tables, we arranged them in the ER Diagram as the foundation for building the database structure and preparing the relationships between the different entities in the next steps.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
